From 7a18810c32157a69dd7a5d3e24c7ceeeb6468676 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sandbox Agent <agent@sandbox.local>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 22:09:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix 524 scan timeout via background job + polling; wire real
 original-video analysis into scan-main-competitors

- New scan_jobs table + lib/scan-jobs.ts: tracks background job status/
  progress. scan-main-competitors/route.ts now returns 202 { jobId }
  immediately instead of blocking for the full scrape+analyze+script
  duration, which previously exceeded Cloudflare's ~100s gateway timeout
  on any scan with more than one or two main competitors (524 error),
  even though the backend kept working and completed successfully anyway.
- New GET /api/viral-ideas/scan-status/[jobId] endpoint for polling.
- Frontend (viral-ideas/page.tsx): replaced the old DB-diffing heuristic
  with real job-status polling every 3s, showing live progress in the
  button label.
- New lib/video-analysis.ts: analyzeOriginalVideo() - real Gemini video
  analysis when GEMINI_API_KEY is configured, with a text-based
  inference fallback via opencode-go when Gemini isn't available.
- scan-main-competitors/route.ts now calls analyzeOriginalVideo() for
  each newly scraped video and saves via new csv.ts helper
  updateVideoAnalysis() - this is what previously stayed hardcoded as
  analysis: "" forever, causing the Original tab, Side-by-Side, and
  hook/body/CTA extraction to always show placeholder text.

Requires GEMINI_API_KEY in .env for real video analysis (free tier
works - Flash/Flash-Lite support video understanding at no cost).
Without it, videos still get analysis via the text-fallback path.
